        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "We are delighted to introduce to the market a distinguished period residence in one of Ireland's most spectacular coastal setting.\r\n\r\nOccupying an elevated position overlooking the magnificent waters of Killary Fjord, The Convent is an outstanding detached residence of remarkable character and scale situated along Ireland's renowned Wild Atlantic Way.\r\n\r\nOriginally constructed as a convent, this unique property has been sympathetically restored and adapted to create an impressive family home extending to approximately 359 sq.m, offering a rare combination of period charm, generous accommodation and breathtaking natural surroundings.\r\n\r\nSet amidst mature grounds with uninterrupted views towards Ireland's only fjord and the surrounding Connemara mountains, The Convent presents a unique opportunity to acquire a landmark property in one of the country's most sought-after scenic locations.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is exceptionally spacious and well-balanced throughout, centred around a series of impressive reception rooms, each enjoying an abundance of natural light and a strong connection to the surrounding landscape. Two elegant drawing rooms with open fireplaces provide inviting spaces for relaxation, while a bright sunroom offers the perfect vantage point from which to enjoy the spectacular fjord views throughout the seasons. The first floor also has a WC and a store.\r\n\r\nA particularly striking feature of the home is the substantial dining room, enhanced by beautiful original stained-glass windows, creating a distinctive and atmospheric setting.\r\n\r\nThe extensive kitchen and service areas have been designed with practicality in mind and include a large fitted kitchen, pantry, utility facilities, storage areas and ancillary accommodation ideally suited to modern family requirements.\r\n\r\nThe first floor provides superb bedroom accomodation comprising of the primary bedroom, two double bedroom and two twin bedrooms-four of the bedrooms are ensuite. There is also a WC and the primarty bathroom on this floor. Each bedroom is generously proportioned and enjoys excellent natural light, while the layout offers an ideal balance of privacy and comfort for family members and guests.\r\n\r\nThe Convent sits on a mature, private site with amble parking and a detached garden.\r\n\r\nFew properties can boast such an exceptional location. Positioned on the edge of the charming village of Leenane, The Convent enjoys commanding views over Killary Fjord, one of Ireland's most dramatic natural landscapes. The surrounding area is renowned for its rugged beauty, outdoor pursuits and vibrant tourism offering. Residents can enjoy easy access to scenic walking routes, fjord cruises, water sports, fishing, cycling and some of Connemara's most celebrated attractions, including Kylemore Abbey and Connemara National Park.\r\n\r\nLeenane itself offers a welcoming selection of cafés, restaurants, traditional pubs and local amenities, along with the very attractive recent addition of a community park, which has an excellent walking/cycle loop and play areas for childred.\r\n\r\nThe Convent represents a truly unique opportunity to acquire a substantial period residence of exceptional character in one of Ireland's most iconic coastal locations. Combining history, space, privacy and unparalleled views, this landmark property offers an enviable lifestyle opportunity on the Wild Atlantic Way.\r\n\r\nThese particulars are intended to give a fair description of the property only and are in no way guaranteed, nor do they form part of any contract. They are issued on the express condition that all negotiations are conducted through Matt O’Sullivan Ltd. All properties are offered subject to contract and to being unsold."
